BT 1 0 0 1 0 85.3 Tm /F1 8.3 Tf 10.4 TL (Quick separation of look-alikes: yellow oily spots on young leaves with white downy growth underneath, and shrivelled brown) Tj T* (clusters, point to downy mildew; grey-white dusty coating on both leaf surfaces, corky or cracked berries, points to powdery) Tj T* (mildew; small dark sunken berry lesions with dark margins \(bird's-eye\), shot-holed leaves and grey-black cane cankers point to) Tj T* (anthracnose; water-soaked angular spots along veins on the underside of leaves in warm humid weather point to bacterial leaf) Tj T* (spot; yellowish marginal leaf spots with concentric brown rings, plus dark patches on rachis and bunch stalk, point to Alternaria;) Tj T* (grey fuzzy rot or watery rot appearing in storage points to Botrytis, Aspergillus or Rhizopus; orange powdery pustules under the) Tj T* (leaf point to rust; reddish-brown leaf spots with black scabby, mummified berries point to black rot; water-soaked leaf lesions) Tj T* (across veins with white-then-black canes point to bitter rot; and angular spots on canes that join into brown areas, with drying) Tj T* (canes, point to dead arm.) Tj T* ET
